import GenMarkoff.General.Assembly.ExplicitStrongApproximation

/-!
# Strong approximation for generalized Markoff surfaces

This library studies the generalized Markoff surfaces
`x₁² + x₂² + x₃² + a₁x₂x₃ + a₂x₃x₁ + a₃x₁x₂ = (3 + a₁ + a₂ + a₃)x₁x₂x₃`
for a fixed integral coefficient triple `a` with `3 + a₁ + a₂ + a₃ ≠ 0` and
`aᵢ² ≠ 4` (`GenMarkoff.IntegrallyNondegenerate`).  For every prime `p` beyond
the explicit cutoff
`GenMarkoff.General.Assembly.explicitStrongApproximationCutoff a`, it proves:

* the group generated by the three Vieta involutions acts transitively on the
  surface modulo `p` with the origin removed
  (`GenMarkoff.IntegrallyNondegenerate.vietaStrongApproximationAt_of_explicitCutoff`);
* the same holds for the group generated by the three two-Vieta rotations
  (`GenMarkoff.IntegrallyNondegenerate.rotationStrongApproximationAt_of_explicitCutoff`);
* coordinatewise reduction from integral solutions onto solutions modulo `p`
  is surjective
  (`GenMarkoff.IntegrallyNondegenerate.reduction_surjective_of_explicitCutoff`).

The qualitative transitivity statement adapts the generic branch of
Kingsbury-Neuschotz (arXiv:2603.04096v3, Theorem 4.3); orbit divisibility by
`p` is the generic branch of de Courcy-Ireland–Litman–Mizuno
(arXiv:2509.02187v3, Theorem 1.1).  This root module imports the file
containing these results, `GenMarkoff.General.Assembly.ExplicitStrongApproximation`.
-/
